        "original_id": "f4bdd9a0-68cb-5859-a76d-b04e87543baf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lower Lake Stone Jail, Sulphur Bank Mine, Eastlake, Lower Lake, Lake County, California\n- Topics: quicksilver operations, mercury production, town growth, civil order\n\nFacts:\n- From 1873 to 1883, the first quicksilver operations of the Sulphur Bank Mine drove rapid town growth and created an urgent need for civil order that necessitated building the Lower Lake Stone Jail.\n- The Sulphur Bank Mine covered 150 acres and became one of the most noted mercury producers in the world.\n- Eastlake, in Lake County, California, was located just southwest of the Sulphur Bank Mine and 7 miles north-northwest of Lower Lake at an elevation of 1,355 feet (413 meters).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
